package engine

var delegationDescriptions = map[string]string{
	"spawn_agent": "Delegate a bounded task when the user, work mode or team instructions allow it. To run independent foreground tasks together, issue their calls in the same response. Extra children queue at the concurrency limit. Foreground results arrive automatically before the parent continues, unless the user steers the parent while it waits. Use background only for work this turn does not depend on; its completion arrives separately. A queued receipt means the child was admitted. Use its returned session and turn IDs to refer to that work.\n\n" +
		"Give the child the goal, relevant context, scope and expected result because it has its own conversation. Choose a role by its exact listed key, or omit role to use this turn's model, even when no roles are configured. Children inherit the worktree, mode and permissions. A named read-only role runs in Plan. Children cannot delegate. A registered worktree or disjoint file scope keeps parallel edits separate.\n\n" +
		"Use guide_agent for follow-ups to an existing child. To start another task with spawn_agent in an idle child, pass its exact returned session ID and omit role to keep its role, model, worktree, settings and history.",
	"guide_agent": "Give new directions to a child owned by this conversation. Copy its exact returned session ID; never reconstruct it. Running guidance is durable: the child receives it after its entire current tool batch settles and before its next model request; an in-flight model response yields at that boundary. This returns a queued guidance receipt, not the child's final result. Explicit follow-up to an idle child starts a new foreground task in the same session, preserving its history, role, model, worktree and permissions. The task uses current package settings. Busy queued or stopping children cannot be restarted.",
	"wait_agent":  "Observe a child owned by this conversation within a bounded observation window and collect its durable final status and answer when available. An admitted, pending response with queued or running status is not failure or completion: the same child continues under its existing session and turn IDs. Do not spawn it again. Use it when the user requests waiting or result collection, or to collect the complete answer from a background notice. Do not poll running background work; its completion arrives as a notice. Guiding background work alone does not request waiting. Copy its exact returned session ID; never reconstruct it. Main-session guidance returns early with guidance_pending so this conversation can apply the user's direction; resume waiting only if the user still requests it. This does not create or replay work.",
}
